":73,"winningTimeRank":49,"winningTimeRankDir":21,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1952,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"07:00:02"}},"narrative":"The 1992 Comrades Marathon was the 67th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 86.700 km. The race was held on Sunday, 31 May. Conditions: Cool at start. Mild to warm later. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nJetman MSUTHU claimed the men's title in 05:46:11, ahead of Mark PAGE (05:48:58) and Shaun MEIKLEJOHN (05:49:37). Frances VAN BLERK won the women's race in 06:51:05, followed by Tilda TEARLE (07:07:44).\n\nFrances VAN BLERK's 06:51:05 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nFrom a field of 13,226 entries, 10,688 runners crossed the finish line (80.8% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,816 men and 872 women (8.2% female). The average finish time was 09:32:27.\n\nMedals awarded: 13 Gold, 845 Silver, 9,830 Bronze. 2,957 runners (27.7%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Marina HELBERG in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1990, the field was 13.9% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 29% of the finishers, with 7,640 seniors (avg 09:27:41) and 3,048 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}